  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of equal mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> are moving with the same speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in figure. They collide completely inelastic&nbsp;and move as a single particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>. The angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> that the path of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> makes with the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis is given by-<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2f77aadb-c7a3-4d0b-a453-4730df6a0169-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 261px;\" />",
